A_SOC_4.1.3_b6","PPP::AQA::7192","PPP::Deck::atomic","PPP::Paper::Paper1","PPP::Topic::theory-and-methods","PPP::Class::background"],"p":"AQA A-level Sociology 7192 – Background knowledge::Paper 1: Education with theory and methods::Theory and methods::4.1.3 (6) Consensus, conflict, structural and social action theories"},{"k":"ppp-soc-7192-background:beea4be4e079a63affb8","f":"What is a metanarrative?","b":"A broad theory claiming to explain society as a whole","t":["PPP::Spec::AQA_SOC_4.1.3_b7","PPP::AQA::7192","PPP::Deck::atomic","PPP::Paper::Paper1","PPP::Topic::theory-and-methods","PPP::Class::background"],"p":"AQA A-level Sociology 7192 – Background knowledge::Paper 1: Education with theory and methods::Theory and methods::4.1.3 (7) The concepts of modernity and post-modernity in relation to sociological theory"},{"k":"ppp-soc-7192-background:883240970f93480aa10e","f":"What is a hypothesis?","b":"A testable proposed explanation","t":["PPP::Spec::AQA_SOC_4.1.3_b8","PPP::AQA::7192","PPP::Deck::atomic","PPP::Paper::Paper1","PPP::Topic::theory-and-methods","PPP::Class::background"],"p":"AQA A-level Sociology 7192 – Background knowledge::Paper 1: Education with theory and methods::Theory and methods::4.1.3 (8) The nature of science and the extent to which Sociology can be regarded as scientific"},{"k":"ppp-soc-7192-background:d930ca8d9dfa15dbf05c","f":"What is a theoretical perspective?","b":"A framework for explaining social life","t":["PPP::Spec::AQA_SOC_4.1.3_b9","PPP::AQA::7192","PPP::Deck::atomic","PPP::Paper::Paper1","PPP::Topic::theory-and-methods","PPP::Class::background"],"p":"AQA A-level Sociology 7192 – Background knowledge::Paper 1: Education with theory and methods::Theory and methods::4.1.3 (9) The relationship between theory and methods"},{"k":"ppp-soc-7192-background:12865038aac5fe44ec56","f":"What is subjectivity in research?","b":"Influence of a researcher’s personal values or standpoint","t":["PPP::Spec::AQA_SOC_4.1.3_b10","PPP::AQA::7192","PPP::