 is domestic labour?","b":"Unpaid work maintaining a household and caring for its members","t":["PPP::Spec::AQA_SOC_4.2.2_b3","PPP::AQA::7192","PPP::Deck::atomic","PPP::Paper::Paper2","PPP::Topic::families-and-households","PPP::Class::background"],"p":"AQA A-level Sociology 7192 – Background knowledge::Paper 2: Topics in sociology::Families and households::4.2.2 (3) Gender roles, domestic labour and power relationships within the family in contemporary society"},{"k":"ppp-soc-7192-background:e88daebc275dc24344a6","f":"What is the social construction of childhood?","b":"The idea that childhood varies across societies and history","t":["PPP::Spec::AQA_SOC_4.2.2_b4","PPP::AQA::7192","PPP::Deck::atomic","PPP::Paper::Paper2","PPP::Topic::families-and-households","PPP::Class::background"],"p":"AQA A-level Sociology 7192 – Background knowledge::Paper 2: Topics in sociology::Families and households::4.2.2 (4) The nature of childhood, and changes in the status of children in the family and society"},{"k":"ppp-soc-7192-background:510bd5f1ed6aece3935a","f":"What is an ageing population?","b":"A rising proportion of older people in a population","t":["PPP::Spec::AQA_SOC_4.2.2_b5","PPP::AQA::7192","PPP::Deck::atomic","PPP::Paper::Paper2","PPP::Topic::families-and-households","PPP::Class::background"],"p":"AQA A-level Sociology 7192 – Background knowledge::Paper 2: Topics in sociology::Families and households::4.2.2 (5) Demographic trends in the United Kingdom since 1900: birth rates, death rates, family size, life expectancy, ageing population, and migration and globalisation"},{"k":"ppp-soc-7192-background:327bda020d69d99f9c89","f":"What is ideology?","b":"A set of ideas that explains or justifies a social order","t":["PPP::Spec::AQA_SOC_4.2.5_b1","PPP::AQA::7192","PPP::Deck::atomic","PPP::Paper::Paper2","PPP::Topic::beliefs-in-society","PPP::Class::background"],"p":"AQA A-level Sociology 7192 – Background knowledge::Paper 2: Topics in sociology::Beliefs in society::4.2.5 (1) Ideology, science and religion, including both Christian and non-Christian religious traditions"},{"k":"ppp-soc-7192-background:a4efe03d8b46f2dfed23","f":"What is the sacred for Durkheim?","b":"Things set apart and treated as special","t":["PPP::Spec::AQA_SOC_4.2.5_b1","PPP::AQA::7192","PPP::Deck::atomic","PPP::Paper::Paper2","PPP::Topic::beliefs-in-society","PPP::Class::background"],"p":"AQA A-level Sociology 7192 – Background knowledge::Paper 2: Topics in sociology::Beliefs in society::4.2.5 (1) Ideology, science and religion, including both Christian and non-Christian religious traditions"},{"k":"ppp-soc-7192-background:3fb5d1d156fc9f00a009","f":"What is social stability?","b":"Continuity and order in social relationships and institutions","t":["PPP::Spec::AQA_SOC_4.2.5_b2","PPP::AQA::7192","PPP::Deck::atomic","PPP::Paper::Paper2","PPP::Topic::beliefs-in-society","PPP::Class::background"],"p":"AQA A-level Sociology 7192 – Background knowledge::Paper 2: Topics in sociology::Beliefs in society::4.2.5 (2) The relationship between social change and social stability, and religious beliefs, practices and organisations"},{"k":"ppp-soc-7192-background:f8a1411a06dfbd6764db","f":"What is a sect in sociology of religion?","b":"A small, exclusive religious group in tension with society","t":["PPP::Spec::AQA_SOC_4.2.5_b3","PPP::AQA::7192","PPP::Deck::atomic","PPP::Paper::Paper2","PPP::Topic::beliefs-in-society","PPP::Class::background"],"p":"AQA A-level Sociology 7192 – Background knowledge::Paper 2: Topics in sociology::Beliefs in society::4.2.5 (3) Religious organisations, including cults, sects, denominations, churches and New Age movements, and their relationship to religious and spiritual belief and practice"},{"k":"ppp-soc-7192-background:43121b4aa01000337656","f":"What is religiosity?","b":"The extent and form of religious belief and practice","t":["PPP::Spec::AQA_SOC_4.2.5_b4","PPP::AQA::7192","PPP::Deck::atomic","PPP::Paper::Paper2","PPP::Topic::beliefs-in-society","P